{
	"_comment": [
		"M3's published tonal palettes, transcribed from material.io.",
		"",
		"These are tables Google publishes, not values computed here. That matters:",
		"material-color-utilities recomputes the same tones and rounds them",
		"differently -- measured against baseline primary, the seed tone lands",
		"exactly and every other tone drifts, up to two steps per channel at tone",
		"50 (#8069BF against the published #7F67BE). So where a published table",
		"exists it wins, and scripts/generate-palette.mjs is for seeds that have",
		"none.",
		"",
		"baseline: the six palettes the scheme is built from. The parent theme",
		"already ships these in tokens.ref.css; they are here to check against and",
		"to diff a transformation, NOT to be re-declared in this child.",
		"",
		"static: M3 Expressive's static palettes. These are the ones worth reaching",
		"for -- a semantic colour a product needs that the scheme does not carry.",
		"Note their tone stops differ from baseline's: 98/95/90/80... with no 99,",
		"and no intermediate neutral stops.",
		"",
		"Static Red is not the same palette as baseline Error. Red 40 is #B3251E",
		"against Error 40 #B3261E, Red 90 is #FFDADC against #F9DEDC. Warmer and",
		"more saturated throughout."
	],

